From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bonsai-27b-fusion <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kvmem): fuse KVMem tiered KV memory adapter into PrismML
 turboquant fusion

- vendor kvmem v0.16.0-rc3 out-of-tree adapter (src/adapter, kvmem/, tools/kvmem,
  tests/kvmem, docs/kvmem, patches/kvmem)
- replay llama-kvmem-current.patch: 38 files, 29 clean hunks applied as-is
- hand-resolve the 14 hunks that collided with PrismML's turboquant/GDN tree:
  * ggml.h/ggml.c/ggml-cpu.c/ggml-cuda.cu: new GGML_OP_GATED_DELTA_NET_RECORD op
    (PrismML already carried the op count; only the name/symbol tables and the
    dispatch cases were missing)
  * ggml-cpu/ops.cpp: K >= 0 and K != 1 scratch selection (RECORD has no state)
  * gated_delta_net.cu: guard the state output pointer for K == 0; keep PrismML's
    column-sharded kernel instead of the upstream single-column helper refactor
  * llama-kv-cells.h/kv-cache.cpp: llama_kv_cell_ext::logical_pos + populate it
    from ubatch.logical_pos (KVMem reads it back as the cache row identity)
  * llama-memory-recurrent.cpp: replay scratch sizing, replay_l tensors
  * delta-net-base.cpp: replay-aware K, k/v/g/b record copies, K>0 fused-node guards

Known gap: the GPU stage-in fast path (llama-kvmem-stagein.cu) is CUDA-only in
upstream KVMem; the HIP/ROCm build needs a compat shim.
